WEBVTT

00:01.070 --> 00:03.130
At the dawn of the Seika era,

00:03.130 --> 00:06.230
in order to regulate unwanted messages that presented a bad influence to society,

00:06.230 --> 00:08.320
the Media Cleansing Act was passed.

00:08.320 --> 00:11.780
The libraries armed themselves in order to protect freedom of expression

00:11.780 --> 00:14.540
from the extreme censorship of the Media Cleansing Committee.

00:14.540 --> 00:17.570
The conflict between the two continued to escalate.

00:17.570 --> 00:24.460
In the 31st year of Seika, a girl who was out of her mind accidentally plunged herself into the middle of that conflict.

00:24.460 --> 00:27.010
It wasn't accidental!

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
usu murasaki hirogaru

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
The faint purple spreads across the sky

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
orenji iro ni kawaru mado no soto

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
The color changes to orange outside the window

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
yoru wa mou bai bai

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
The night's already "bye-bye"

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
tada kirei na mono wo kirei to

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
I just want to be someone who

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
ieru atashi de itai

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
calls beautiful things beautiful

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
ima wa dokidoki shitai no

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
I want to get excited for it!

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
fumidashichae tomaranai

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
So I step out, unstoppable

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
zenbu te ni hairi sou de

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
And take everything into my own hands

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
sono saki de aitai

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
Beyond there, I want to meet

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
mita koto no nai atashi

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
the new self that I've never seen

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
sayonara daisuki na machi

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
Farewell, my beloved town

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
atashi mo ganbatte miru yo

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
I'll try to do my best

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
kono sora no tsuzuku basho de

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
somewhere under the same sky

01:48.870 --> 01:53.430
U-Um, you are my prince.

01:53.430 --> 01:56.710
Please, at least tell me your name!

02:07.960 --> 02:09.390
Instructor Dojo?

02:09.920 --> 02:11.680
You idiot!

02:11.680 --> 02:13.640
Get back to your duties!

02:18.970 --> 02:23.420
Situation 09

02:18.970 --> 02:23.420
Approaching the
Preferment Exam

02:27.980 --> 02:29.910
What's up with her?

02:29.910 --> 02:32.370
She's been like that since last night.

02:32.810 --> 02:36.330
I asked her why, but she wouldn't tell me.

02:37.260 --> 02:39.040
I couldn't possibly tell anyone

02:39.760 --> 02:42.500
that the object of my admiration was Instructor Dojo,

02:42.500 --> 02:46.790
and that I've been calling him my prince!

02:48.250 --> 02:51.850
This is what's troubling you, isn't it?

02:52.530 --> 02:54.900
Huh? The Preferment Exam?

02:55.640 --> 02:58.800
You're all Librarians First Class, so you'll be taking one for Chief Librarian.

02:59.310 --> 03:03.570
Whether you pass or fail will depend on a combination of written and practical exams.

03:03.570 --> 03:06.280
The pass rate is about 50%.

03:06.280 --> 03:07.710
50%?

03:07.710 --> 03:09.690
Only half pass?

03:09.690 --> 03:11.840
As many as 50%?

03:11.840 --> 03:13.170
A piece of cake.

03:13.170 --> 03:18.500
That's the kind of thing only people who grew up unaffected by the competitiveness of exams can say!

03:18.500 --> 03:19.960
Right...

03:19.960 --> 03:23.500
You might have a tough time with the written exam.

03:24.670 --> 03:29.390
You should pass the Chief Librarian Exam if you memorize this whole book.

03:29.390 --> 03:32.040
Memorize this whole thing?

03:32.040 --> 03:33.430
Impossible.

03:33.430 --> 03:35.310
Don't worry.

03:35.820 --> 03:37.850
I'll coach the written exam.

03:44.450 --> 03:46.500
What are you doing?

03:46.500 --> 03:47.070
Are you okay?

03:48.070 --> 03:50.490
I'm fine!

03:58.270 --> 04:01.510
It's not every day that you ask me for advice.

04:01.510 --> 04:04.140
I'm not really asking for advice.

04:04.970 --> 04:06.610
So, what do you need?

04:06.610 --> 04:08.590
Well, it's about...

04:08.590 --> 04:10.280
Spit it out.

04:10.280 --> 04:14.030
You want to know how to get ready for the practical exam, right?

04:14.030 --> 04:15.640
You already knew?

04:16.110 --> 04:20.330
Why is this year's practical exam reading a book to kids?

04:20.330 --> 04:24.920
It's like they knew I'm horrible at this!

04:25.820 --> 04:28.330
Won't it be completely embarrassing

04:28.330 --> 04:31.570
if Kasahara passes and you fail?

04:32.750 --> 04:34.530
If it really happens...

04:35.520 --> 04:37.590
Don't say that!

04:37.590 --> 04:40.570
I wouldn't mind teaching you.

04:40.570 --> 04:41.490
Really?

04:41.490 --> 04:45.390
The Operations Department often hosts events for kids.

04:45.390 --> 04:48.300
I'll make a deal for it.

04:49.990 --> 04:51.760
A cake set or something?

04:52.210 --> 04:54.630
One full course dinner.

04:54.630 --> 04:56.220
Drinks included, of course.

05:01.190 --> 05:04.810
Users are limited to checking out ten books at a time.

05:05.530 --> 05:08.320
The limit is five for audio or video items.

05:08.320 --> 05:16.520
However, audio and video items are limited to junior high students, or anyone 15 years of age or older who also holds a library card.

05:14.580 --> 05:17.440
I'm such an idiot!

05:17.440 --> 05:21.620
How could I not have noticed that the person I admire was so close to me?

05:21.620 --> 05:23.330
Not only that...

05:26.500 --> 05:29.460
No! So embarrassing!

05:29.460 --> 05:32.340
Are you listening to me?

05:35.550 --> 05:37.150
Shoot!

05:37.150 --> 05:39.120
I can't even maintain eye contact!

05:39.120 --> 05:40.460
Are you okay, Kasahara?

05:40.460 --> 05:42.190
You're all flushed.

05:42.190 --> 05:43.910
I'm okay!

05:43.910 --> 05:45.150
Maybe you have a fever?

05:46.490 --> 05:48.110
I'm fine!

05:50.060 --> 05:52.630
Really, I'm fine.

05:53.040 --> 05:55.100
Let me go get some coffee.

05:55.100 --> 05:57.090
I'm thirsty.

06:00.160 --> 06:03.540
I wonder what he'd think of it?

06:03.540 --> 06:06.930
The way I made him into a prince?

06:06.930 --> 06:09.090
I'm sure he wouldn't welcome it.

06:25.350 --> 06:26.690
What the hell is this?

06:26.690 --> 06:28.790
How much sugar did you put in it?

06:28.790 --> 06:30.860
Were you a stag beetle or something in your previous life?

06:31.640 --> 06:32.600
No way.

06:36.770 --> 06:38.140
I'm sorry!

06:38.140 --> 06:39.830
I wasn't paying attention!

06:40.570 --> 06:41.210
Are you okay?

06:41.210 --> 06:41.990
I'm sorry!

06:41.990 --> 06:43.950
Let me clean it up!

06:46.910 --> 06:48.130
What's this?

06:48.130 --> 06:49.590
A letter?

06:50.480 --> 06:52.190
That's...

06:53.980 --> 06:57.080
It's 20,000 yen that Tezuka's brother sent back.

06:57.080 --> 06:58.430
I wanted to give it back to you.

06:58.810 --> 07:00.260
What did he say to you?

07:01.800 --> 07:03.120
What's in that letter?

07:03.120 --> 07:06.770
Is that letter the reason you're not being yourself?

07:06.770 --> 07:10.050
It doesn't have much.

07:10.050 --> 07:11.230
Just let me see it.

07:11.930 --> 07:14.360
Really, it's got nothing to do with you.

07:14.360 --> 07:16.240
This is happening right after the last incident.

07:16.240 --> 07:18.860
I'll make the decisions regarding Tezuka Satoshi!

07:18.860 --> 07:19.590
Please don't!

07:19.590 --> 07:20.120
Let me see it!

07:20.120 --> 07:21.530
Instructor Dojo!

07:21.530 --> 07:23.290
Let me see it!

07:24.630 --> 07:27.120
Stop it!

07:29.720 --> 07:31.510
Instructor Dojo?

07:31.510 --> 07:32.880
My body acted on its own!

07:32.880 --> 07:34.220
Oh no! Answer me!

07:34.220 --> 07:35.730
Don't die!

07:40.790 --> 07:42.600
How is he?

07:42.600 --> 07:43.490
He's fine.

07:43.490 --> 07:45.440
He just has a minor concussion.

07:45.440 --> 07:48.160
She said he'll wake up on his own after an hour or so.

07:48.600 --> 07:50.690
Thank goodness!

07:50.690 --> 07:57.230
In any case, you must have had a good reason to throw him in a way he couldn't recover from!

07:57.230 --> 07:58.590
Well...

07:58.590 --> 08:02.910
Would you tell me if it's something you couldn't tell Dojo?

08:05.290 --> 08:09.150
Can you please keep this from Instructor Dojo?

08:10.220 --> 08:11.380
Of course.

08:15.450 --> 08:21.430
I've compared him to my prince so many times.

08:21.430 --> 08:24.960
No wonder he hates me.

08:25.300 --> 08:26.940
Wait a minute.

08:26.940 --> 08:28.420
How did you come to that conclusion?

08:29.640 --> 08:36.230
Because he looked very irritated when I talked about my prince.

08:36.860 --> 08:41.570
He doesn't hate you. At least, not as his subordinate...

08:42.040 --> 08:45.710
Actually, he's almost overprotective of you.

08:45.710 --> 08:46.920
But...

08:46.920 --> 08:50.460
why does he speak so badly of my prince, then?

08:51.110 --> 08:56.420
That's only logical if he's trying to make me hate both of them.

08:56.870 --> 08:57.800
Come on.

08:58.230 --> 09:00.100
Calm down a bit.

09:00.100 --> 09:05.020
You're just confused right now after suddenly learning the identity of your prince.

09:07.580 --> 09:12.440
How do you feel when you think about what you were like six years ago?

09:14.220 --> 09:15.400
I'm embarrassed.

09:17.380 --> 09:21.760
Would you feel better if I told you that I feel the same way?

09:21.760 --> 09:23.820
You do?

09:33.600 --> 09:34.640
Instructor Dojo!

09:38.350 --> 09:39.980
I can't.

09:39.980 --> 09:43.030
I know it in my head, but I still can't face him.

09:52.200 --> 09:54.940
Oh yeah! I just remembered something...

09:55.290 --> 09:56.920
About that letter.

09:58.040 --> 09:59.330
That?

09:59.330 --> 10:01.350
I don't care about it anymore.

10:01.350 --> 10:02.670
Please don't worry.

10:02.670 --> 10:04.900
You can't not care about it!

10:04.900 --> 10:07.780
I realized that I had mixed up my professional and private lives.

10:08.570 --> 10:10.450
Really, I don't care about it!

10:10.450 --> 10:12.410
Forget about it!

10:14.920 --> 10:18.870
Jeez, why do I end up like this?

10:22.580 --> 10:23.960
I'm back.

10:23.960 --> 10:25.120
Welcome back.

10:25.120 --> 10:26.360
You were out late.

10:26.360 --> 10:27.790
Do you want any supper?

10:27.790 --> 10:28.760
No.

10:29.140 --> 10:30.970
I'm going to bed.

10:33.990 --> 10:35.250
He hates me now.

10:35.890 --> 10:38.260
I really made him hate me for sure.

10:47.930 --> 10:50.470
What's going on?

10:50.470 --> 10:51.860
It's story telling time.

10:51.860 --> 10:54.000
Here, help us.

10:55.210 --> 10:56.850
Can you play with me?

10:56.850 --> 10:58.530
No! He's playing with me!

10:58.530 --> 11:00.220
Hey! Wait a minute!

11:00.220 --> 11:00.860
Calm down!

11:00.860 --> 11:02.340
Calm down!

11:03.800 --> 11:06.640
Let's start story time!

11:06.640 --> 11:08.260
Can you come and sit down?

11:08.260 --> 11:11.000
Who's going to be the last one to sit?

11:15.940 --> 11:19.100
Just you watch, Snow White.

11:19.100 --> 11:22.090
Oh my, that's a delicious-looking apple.

11:22.090 --> 11:23.540
I'll take a bite.

11:24.010 --> 11:25.370
Don't eat it!

11:25.370 --> 11:27.500
It's poisonous!

11:27.500 --> 11:32.010
Oh my, who's telling my secret?

11:32.450 --> 11:34.570
No way...

11:34.570 --> 11:38.210
Is this the same woman who pawned my watch?

11:39.860 --> 11:40.980
What did you think?

11:43.480 --> 11:45.020
You were really good.

11:45.020 --> 11:47.180
I can't possibly imitate that.

11:48.120 --> 11:51.740
If you think I'm good, you still have a long way to go.

11:51.740 --> 11:56.330
But at least you learned the point of view of the children.

11:57.080 --> 11:59.190
The point of view of the children?

12:05.360 --> 12:07.000
What's this?

12:10.410 --> 12:14.870
Those are the written exam prep notes you made for Kasahara, aren't they?

12:14.870 --> 12:17.350
I'm not giving them to her!

12:17.350 --> 12:20.030
I made them just in case!

12:20.030 --> 12:21.970
Why don't you give them to her?

12:21.970 --> 12:24.070
I'm sure she'd appreciate it.

12:24.070 --> 12:25.290
No.

12:25.290 --> 12:27.380
I'm sure she hates me.

12:27.380 --> 12:28.660
She hates you?

12:28.660 --> 12:29.930
Who, Kasahara?

12:29.930 --> 12:31.380
Yeah.

12:31.380 --> 12:33.800
She avoided me again the other day.

12:34.310 --> 12:35.350
What's so funny?

12:36.500 --> 12:40.060
I was thinking about how similar you two are.

12:44.980 --> 12:45.740
Damn it!

12:45.740 --> 12:48.200
I can't focus at all.

12:48.200 --> 12:52.660
Maybe it's better for me to pack up and move back home.

13:03.950 --> 13:07.090
What are you doing up so late?

13:07.090 --> 13:09.310
I'm quitting the Library Force and going home.

13:12.040 --> 13:13.940
I'm serious about it!

13:13.940 --> 13:16.050
Go ahead.

13:16.970 --> 13:18.480
You won't stop me?

13:18.480 --> 13:20.490
I said I'm quitting the Library Force.

13:21.020 --> 13:23.130
Say hi to your parents.

13:23.130 --> 13:24.480
Get me something as a souvenir.

13:26.570 --> 13:29.920
At least pretend that you feel for me, idiot!

13:33.950 --> 13:35.030
Wait a minute!

13:35.030 --> 13:37.740
What the hell are you doing in the girls' dorm, you pervert!

13:38.320 --> 13:40.450
No! It's me!

13:41.010 --> 13:42.620
Instructor Dojo?

13:43.100 --> 13:45.110
Why are you here?

13:45.110 --> 13:46.420
Well...

13:49.420 --> 13:50.390
What's this?

13:51.360 --> 13:52.300
That's...

13:56.170 --> 13:57.570
It's...

13:58.300 --> 14:00.640
I summarized the points for the written exam.

14:01.260 --> 14:04.580
For me?

14:04.580 --> 14:05.900
Toss it if you don't need it.

14:05.900 --> 14:07.570
I won't force you to use it.

14:07.980 --> 14:09.730
Thank you!

14:09.730 --> 14:10.690
I really appreciate it!

14:12.200 --> 14:18.420
I wanted to avoid making a laughingstock out of our group by having one person fail the exam.

14:19.390 --> 14:23.160
Man, I was actually going to secretly leave it under the door.

14:27.620 --> 14:29.380
Why are you crying?

14:30.650 --> 14:35.090
Because I thought you'd never talk to me again.

14:36.180 --> 14:37.550
Why would you think that?

14:38.500 --> 14:40.510
Because I thought you hated me.

14:40.510 --> 14:42.820
That's my line!

14:42.820 --> 14:44.730
You're the one who kept avoiding me!

14:57.560 --> 15:02.990
Kasahara, do you know why the sunflower is used in the Library Force's logo?

15:02.990 --> 15:04.290
The sunflower?

15:04.290 --> 15:06.300
Isn't this a chamomile?

15:06.300 --> 15:07.830
A chamomile?

15:07.830 --> 15:09.280
It's also known as that?

15:10.140 --> 15:12.950
It's often used in aromatic oils and herbal teas.

15:12.950 --> 15:15.840
It has a sweet and refreshing fragrance.

15:15.840 --> 15:16.590
I get it!

15:17.040 --> 15:21.240
The flowers on your rank badge are also chamomiles.

15:21.970 --> 15:28.900
Commander Inamine is the one who suggested to use this flower on the rank badges and the Library Force logo.

15:28.900 --> 15:31.360
His late wife liked it.

15:31.880 --> 15:34.400
Commander Inamine's wife, eh...

15:35.210 --> 15:37.990
This flower stands for "Energy in adversity."

15:41.870 --> 15:44.890
Not all of our tasks are fun.

15:44.890 --> 15:46.630
We sometimes go through tough times.

15:47.420 --> 15:51.320
I won't ask what happened between you and Tezuka Satoshi.

15:51.320 --> 15:54.500
But you're still my valuable subordinate.

15:54.500 --> 15:57.120
I will protect you with everything I have if I need to.

15:57.120 --> 15:59.320
Instructor Dojo...

16:02.670 --> 16:05.180
Good luck with your exam.

16:13.000 --> 16:17.800
The Day of the
Preferment Exam

16:14.210 --> 16:17.830
We are now commencing the Preferment Exam for the rank of Chief Librarian.

16:18.260 --> 16:23.260
Written Exam

16:23.950 --> 16:25.860
Story Room

16:24.210 --> 16:28.880
Practical Exam

16:32.950 --> 16:35.760
Testee 156
Shibasaki Asako

16:38.750 --> 16:43.240
Who's being bad?

16:43.240 --> 16:45.940
Give me the scepter.

16:46.800 --> 16:49.890
Let's start story time.

16:49.890 --> 16:52.270
It's the Horse Ghost.

16:52.270 --> 16:56.490
Try drawing the attention of the children by reading lines from a climactic scene.

16:58.040 --> 17:02.670
Testee 157
Tezuka Hikaru

17:02.840 --> 17:05.310
He's so tall!

17:07.720 --> 17:10.030
The children's point of view?

17:10.030 --> 17:10.820
Yup.

17:11.460 --> 17:14.530
No, I just stood because they climbed on me when I was standing...

17:14.530 --> 17:16.750
That's what the children's point of view is.

17:17.610 --> 17:19.100
I get it!

17:19.100 --> 17:22.210
They wanted to climb because they wanted to see from this height.

17:23.530 --> 17:24.780
It's okay.

17:24.780 --> 17:26.290
You can do it.

17:31.600 --> 17:37.190
The fox jumped and jumped, but it couldn't reach the grape.

17:37.190 --> 17:39.740
He should bring a ladder.

17:39.740 --> 17:41.680
Wasn't he smart?

17:43.040 --> 17:49.330
It's not that this fox was stupid, but that you're all very smart instead!

17:49.330 --> 17:53.260
I hope you become people who wouldn't give up on your grape.

17:54.640 --> 17:59.490
Testee 165
Kasahara Iku

18:02.130 --> 18:05.060
Hey kids, we'll do a puzzle together!

18:05.060 --> 18:06.410
Go ahead and open the boxes.

18:06.410 --> 18:08.800
Take everything out of the box!

18:10.900 --> 18:14.270
Can you find the nuts and the leaves drawn on the poster boards?

18:14.270 --> 18:16.150
Find them all!

18:17.180 --> 18:18.300
This is it!

18:18.300 --> 18:19.720
No it's not!

18:22.430 --> 18:23.950
See this?

18:23.950 --> 18:26.820
Sycamore nuts look like this.

18:26.820 --> 18:28.530
And this leaf is from a cherry tree.

18:28.530 --> 18:31.670
These are all trees you see around this library.

18:32.810 --> 18:34.970
How's your student?

18:34.970 --> 18:36.480
Perfect.

18:36.480 --> 18:40.630
It's highly original, and it makes the kids want to learn, of course.

18:40.630 --> 18:42.350
It's a very skillful session.

18:42.740 --> 18:46.310
Results Day

18:54.000 --> 18:55.900
Yeah!

18:55.900 --> 18:58.090
Both your names are on it!

18:58.090 --> 18:59.670
Of course mine is.

18:59.670 --> 19:03.560
I'm aiming to become the first female commander in history.

19:03.560 --> 19:04.090
Seriously?

19:04.890 --> 19:08.070
It doesn't sound like a joke at all coming from her.

19:11.250 --> 19:12.310
Instructor Dojo!

19:15.250 --> 19:18.600
Thank you for the written exam prep notes.

19:18.600 --> 19:20.590
I probably would have failed without them.

19:21.620 --> 19:26.410
You cut it close with the written exam, but you were way ahead of everyone else on the practical exam.

19:26.410 --> 19:29.690
It's unusual for you to take first place.

19:29.690 --> 19:30.300
Enjoy it while you can.

19:30.300 --> 19:32.750
Um, this is for you.

19:32.750 --> 19:35.590
To thank you for the notes.

19:36.390 --> 19:38.500
What's this?

19:38.500 --> 19:40.470
It's chamomile aromatic oil.

19:40.470 --> 19:43.340
You heat it and let it evaporate, then enjoy the fragrance.

19:44.650 --> 19:46.350
Also...

19:47.500 --> 19:49.110
I'm graduating from my prince.

19:51.090 --> 19:56.140
I'll stop searching for my prince and getting excited about him.

19:56.140 --> 20:01.340
I will grow up to be properly recognized by you, and not by my prince.

20:01.870 --> 20:06.300
And I will have the same chamomile as you.

20:07.760 --> 20:09.050
Do as you like.

20:11.630 --> 20:13.250
It smells good.

20:13.250 --> 20:15.520
I like that fragrance too.

20:16.520 --> 20:19.370
By the way, you mentioned a chamomile tea as well.

20:19.370 --> 20:20.860
Yes.

20:20.860 --> 20:24.660
Would you take me to a place where we can have chamomile tea?

20:24.660 --> 20:25.730
Huh?

20:26.190 --> 20:29.200
I want to see it in full blossom as well if possible.

20:29.580 --> 20:31.160
Is this...

20:31.870 --> 20:36.390
Because I had chamomile on my arm, and I still didn't know the real thing.

20:36.390 --> 20:39.640
It's probably a good thing to learn from a teacher who knows about plants.

20:40.030 --> 20:43.560
It's almost like he's asking me out!

20:44.300 --> 20:45.360
What?

20:46.650 --> 20:48.300
I'm sorry!

20:48.300 --> 20:50.260
Excuse me!

20:59.940 --> 21:01.060
Damn it!

21:01.060 --> 21:03.810
I think my heart is going to burst!

21:06.690 --> 21:10.030
nani ka ga kawaru kigashita

21:06.690 --> 21:10.030
I had a feeling something was about to change

21:10.030 --> 21:13.410
nani mo kawaranu asa ni

21:10.030 --> 21:13.410
on this very ordinary morning

21:13.410 --> 21:18.420
itsu mo yori sukoshi ii mezamedatta

21:13.410 --> 21:18.420
I woke up feeling a little better than usual

21:20.080 --> 21:26.760
hito sashiyubi de sashimesu no wa mirai

21:20.080 --> 21:26.760
My index finger points out to the future

21:26.760 --> 21:36.430
kimi no te no hira ga fureru tabi ni afuru omoi

21:26.760 --> 21:36.430
My thoughts overflow each time I touch your palm

21:36.880 --> 21:40.410
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:36.880 --> 21:40.410
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:40.410 --> 21:43.730
sayonara furui jibun

21:40.410 --> 21:43.730
Goodbye my old self

21:43.730 --> 21:50.260
shingenjitsu atarashii nani ka ga matteru

21:43.730 --> 21:50.260
There's something new awaiting me in the new reality

21:50.260 --> 21:54.000
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:50.260 --> 21:54.000
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:54.000 --> 21:57.230
ushinau mono mo aru

21:54.000 --> 21:57.230
There are things I'll lose too

21:57.230 --> 22:03.000
demo iindesu hitotsu unazuki kakedasu

21:57.230 --> 22:03.000
But that's okay, I'll just nod and keep running

22:03.000 --> 22:10.550
saa subete ga ima kawatteku subete ga hajimaru

22:03.000 --> 22:10.550
Yeah, everything is changing now, everything starts now

22:10.550 --> 22:20.840
shingenjitsu dare no mono demo nai atarashii jibun

22:10.550 --> 22:20.840
It's a new reality, my new self belongs to no one but me
